	<content contentuid="hfd8476a8gbca1g4880g97cege37a408b25f8" version="1">Pyre Equilibrium: X</content>
	<content contentuid="h0a580ae8g774eg4e0ag804agb1d9ee74437b" version="1">The step the Pyre is trying to climb to in order to find its &lt;b&gt;balance&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Your &lt;b&gt;magical gear&lt;/b&gt; and even &lt;b&gt;Runic Shards&lt;/b&gt; affect that number, and so does the &lt;b&gt;difficulty mode&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;The Pyre updates &lt;b&gt;once per round&lt;/b&gt;, at the start of the boss's turn (or at the start of the round if the boss is already dead).&lt;br&gt;The Pyre grows faster the more of the enemy's health you take off in a round. A fight that drags on speeds it up on its own.</content>
	<content contentuid="hb93bc457geaffg455bgbe32g96564bdc08a7" version="1">Pyre: Rising</content>
	<content contentuid="h4420b73fgd2beg4a6dgbb2ag90ac91392e28" version="1">The Pyre is rising. Only the abilities against the Pyre, or a fallen party member, will bring it down.</content>
	<content contentuid="h68c31c1dg1b68g4599g88feg007e9f4a6d98" version="1">Pyre: Fading</content>
	<content contentuid="h2cf7c024g3c58g4454gb72fg346cd3b63c88" version="1">The Pyre is fading: a party member is down. It will rise again once everyone is back up.</content>
	<content contentuid="h4f8f2b80geee5g4b8cg9c37g4540a2e28572" version="1">Pyre: Subdued</content>
	<content contentuid="h51075992g8560g40b3ga23fgd562f1af10d5" version="1">The Pyre has been subdued and will not rise again in this fight.</content>
